Chapter: DeskWindowRepaintTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopFont
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A window that ticks repaints itself and whatever is over it, and nothing
 else.

 The Clock's own repaint used to be `desk-wnd-paint-all`: the chrome and every
 open window, redrawn on the visible framebuffer once a second. Nothing
 outside the ticking window had changed, so what that bought was a
 full-screen rebuild at 1 Hz, which a person sees as the whole desk
 flickering the moment two windows are open. Redrawing one window alone is
 wrong only if something sits over it, and the registry's array order IS the z
 order, so the answer is to start the walk at that window's index.

 THE ASSERTION IS THE INDEX AND THE COUNT IT IMPLIES, because the walk itself
 paints and a test cannot read pixels back from a framebuffer it does not
 have. `desk-wnd-index` is what decides how much gets repainted: the number
 of windows from that index to the top is exactly what `desk-wnd-walk` will
 draw. A bottom window still costs every window; a top window costs one; a
 window that was never opened costs nothing at all, which is the arm that
 stops an absent pane from quietly repainting the whole desk.

 The registry is built through `dk-wr-open` rather than poked, so this
 measures the order that machinery actually produces.

Section: Test

  dwr-yn : Boolean -> Text
  dwr-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

  dwr-from : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dwr-from (ws) (fid) =
    let i = desk-wnd-index ws fid 0
    in if i < 0 then 0 else dk-wr-count ws - i

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let ds = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let ap = poke-32 ds dk-adorn-cell dk-adorn-default
    in let wp = poke-32 ds dk-wr-cell (alloc-zeroed 64 64)
    in let ws = peek-32 ds dk-wr-cell
    in let o1 = dk-wr-open ws desk-focus-clkp
    in let o2 = dk-wr-open ws desk-focus-calc
    in let o3 = dk-wr-open ws desk-focus-cal
    in act
      print-line-uni ("open " & integer-to-text (dk-wr-count ws) & ", bottom to top: " & integer-to-text (dk-wr-at ws 0) & " " & integer-to-text (dk-wr-at ws 1) & " " & integer-to-text (dk-wr-at ws 2))
      print-line-uni ("clock at " & integer-to-text (desk-wnd-index ws desk-focus-clkp 0) & " repaints " & integer-to-text (dwr-from ws desk-focus-clkp))
      print-line-uni ("calc  at " & integer-to-text (desk-wnd-index ws desk-focus-calc 0) & " repaints " & integer-to-text (dwr-from ws desk-focus-calc))
      print-line-uni ("cal   at " & integer-to-text (desk-wnd-index ws desk-focus-cal 0) & " repaints " & integer-to-text (dwr-from ws desk-focus-cal))
      print-line-uni ("never opened: index " & integer-to-text (desk-wnd-index ws desk-focus-mon 0) & " repaints " & integer-to-text (dwr-from ws desk-focus-mon))
      print-line-uni ("the top window costs one: " & dwr-yn (dwr-from ws (dk-wr-top ws) == 1))
    end

